      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, the detail helps a lot. I think we're getting closer to what we need.\n\nI was just looking at the draft again and I'm still a little nervous about that dashboard. I did a quick mental check of the keywords and I'm worried the density might be a bit too low to actually trigger the \"green\" status on the HR side. \n\nCan you do one more pass to make it a full, comprehensive report? I need you to really dive deep into each department's section. Don't be afraid to use the terminology from the index more frequently if it helps clarify the points—like when discussing the Product team's tools or the Engineering promotion paths—just make sure it still flows like a professional report. I'm really looking for a version that feels comprehensive and \"heavy\" enough to satisfy the metric without looking like a list of words. Basically, make it more robust and ensure those key themes are very clearly present throughout.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
